  "narrative": "All estimates below are already signed to the stated hypothesis direction, so I accepted only when the point estimate exceeded 0.15 composite dependency-score units and the uncertainty was compatible with a threshold-exceeding effect. The new PTEN refinements remain suggestive but immature. H87, PTEN loss in TP53-wildtype, Avana-library, high-screen-quality samples, gives signed estimate +0.195 with interval +0.068 to +0.323; H88, PTEN loss in high-quality Avana samples without TP53 restriction, gives +0.191 with interval +0.059 to +0.322; H89, PTEN loss in TP53-wildtype high-aneuploidy samples, gives +0.206 but with wide interval +0.031 to +0.382 and only 52 exposed cells. These are positive point estimates, but none excludes values below the 0.15-unit threshold, and several have exposed-cell sizes and intervals that make them unreliable as mature claims. Because H40 PTEN-loss in TP53-wildtype already failed independent threshold exclusion, and because the new contexts are multiple borderline tests, I do not request independent validation now; PTEN remains exploratory rather than an accepted dataset-specific predictor. The broad mutation/marker scans do not support additional accepted claims. EGFR amplification H33 is signed negative and opposite the claimed stronger-dependency direction with interval crossing zero; ERBB2 amplification H34, BRAF V600E H51, and PIK3CA mutation H35 are all small, below threshold, and interval-compatible with no effect, so I reject and close them. Sex H84 was specified as a positive male-versus-female contrast, but the signed estimate is -0.083, i.e. the opposite direction and below threshold in absolute magnitude, so the claimed positive association is rejected and closed; the observed sex contrast is too small to qualify as scientifically meaningful. Technical context indicators also do not support important associations in the claimed direction: Avana-library H76 has signed estimate +0.053 with upper bound +0.141 below threshold, and matched omics/CRISPR-QC H77 is negative and far below threshold; both are rejected and closed, which reduces concern that library or omics-QC status explains the large validated associations by itself. The follow-up interaction tests do not support threshold-level context dependence: H90 SMARCA4-loss association is not meaningfully amplified by high aneuploidy (signed estimate -0.027, interval crossing zero), and H92 KEAP1-loss association is not meaningfully modified by SMARCA4 loss (signed estimate -0.018, interval crossing zero). I reject and close both. The mature dataset-specific conclusions remain the large associations for SMARCA4 loss toward stronger dependency, TP53 loss toward weaker dependency, and KEAP1 loss toward weaker dependency. PTEN is a moderate positive signal but still exploratory. I request no validation this stage because no new PTEN claim clears the threshold, H40 validation already failed to support threshold-level TP53-wildtype PTEN, and validating another borderline PTEN refinement now risks allocating the validation budget without a mature candidate.",
  "research_notes": "Mature accepted/closed dataset-specific associations remain H3 SMARCA4 loss -> stronger dependency; H13 TP53 loss -> weaker dependency; H38 KEAP1 loss -> weaker dependency. PTEN remains exploratory after new refinements: H87 TP53-wt+Avana+high ROC +0.195 lower +0.068; H88 Avana+high ROC +0.191 lower +0.059; H89 TP53-wt+high aneuploidy +0.206 lower +0.031 with small exposed n. None clears threshold with interval; no validation requested because H40 already failed validation and PTEN claims are multiple borderline. Null/closed broad technical or genomic comparisons: EGFR H33, ERBB2 H34, BRAF H51, PIK3CA H35, positive-sex H84, Avana-library H76, matched omics/CRISPR-QC H77, SMARCA4-by-aneuploidy interaction H90, KEAP1-by-SMARCA4 interaction H92. Sex male-female raw contrast is negative but below threshold; not accepted. Next continue diverse exploration and use unanalyzed registered claims (e.g., H85, H86, H91, H93) or other measured predictors; keep PTEN active/deferred only if future analyses produce a mature subgroup with interval above threshold. Interpret all findings as dataset-specific associations, not causal effects or generalizable biology."
